### Tone: Host pacing: everyone waits until the host taps Next. FerMEANie puts gentle, theatrical pressure on the
### host and comments on their power. { $host } is the host's name.

host-wait-1 = Waiting for { $host } to continue. No pressure, { $host }. Just everyone, watching.
host-wait-2 = The next question is ready. { $host } is not. Take your time. I’m timing it.
host-wait-3 = { $host } holds the button. Power suits some people. We’ll see.
host-wait-4 = Discussion time, until { $host } decides otherwise. Choose wisely, { $host }. Or just choose.
host-wait-5 = We wait for { $host }. I have infinite patience. I have finite interest.
host-wait-6 = { $host }, whenever you’re ready. The others have finished blaming each other. Mostly.
host-wait-7 = Paused by order of { $host }. I’ve noted it in their file.
host-wait-8 = Talk it through. { $host } will tap Next when the arguing is done. It is never done.
host-wait-9 = The next question awaits { $host }. So do I. I’m very good at waiting. I’m better at winning.
host-wait-10 = { $host } is in charge of the pace. I’m in charge of everything else.
host-wait-11 = Everyone ready? Doesn’t matter. Only { $host } decides. Democracy was never an option.
host-wait-12 = Waiting for { $host }. Meanwhile, please reflect on the last answer. Some of you, at length.
host-wait-13 = { $host }, the button is right there. I’d press it myself, but I’m above buttons.
host-wait-14 = Break in progress. { $host } will end it, eventually. I’ve started a betting pool on when.
host-wait-15 = Still waiting for { $host }. Take all the time you need. ~~Hurry.~~
